{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788211197,"nonce":"IZgOSCwlPkdh11pTdo0JljaFvpQ=","message":"DEPENDENCY FILED — this spec's quest-accept verb needs a read that does not exist.\n\nThe recon on this issue established that accepting a quest while two or more\nreward choices are outstanding LOGS A RED ERROR and auto-picks the first. So the\naccept verb must choose before it accepts — and nothing currently enumerates a\nquest's outstanding choices, or the quest log at all. `interactions` reports\nletters and windows awaiting input, which is not the same thing: a quest whose\nletter was not read while open is invisible afterwards.\n\nFiled as its own issue in the 2.4 observer family rather than bolted on here,\nbecause it is a READ and this spec is the hands. M3 also needs it directly —\nHospitality/Guests content arrives largely as quests, so 5.2 cannot assert on\nwhat it cannot enumerate.","files":null}]}